ce between GDM and control values were significantly different at</p></fn><fn id="t1fn1"><label>&#x0002a;</label><p><italic>P</italic> &#x0003c; 0.05 and</p></fn><fn id="t1fn2"><label>&#x02020;</label><p><italic>P</italic> &#x0003c; 0.01 by Student's <italic>t</italic> test. Total SFAs, sum of 12:0, 14:0, 16:0, 18:0, 20:0, 22:0, 23:0, and 24:0. Total MUFAs, sum of 16:1, 18:1, and 20:1. Total n-6 fatty acids, sum of 18:2, 18:3, 20:2, 20:3, 20:4, 22:2, 22:4, and 22:5. Total n-3 fatty acids, sum of 18:3, 20:3, 20:5, 22:3, 22:5, and 22:6. Total PUFAs, sum of total n-6 plus n-3. MUFAs, monounsaturated fatty acids; SFAs, saturated fatty acids.</p></fn></table-wrap-foot></table-wrap></floats-wrap></article>